  "title": "How to Solve Quadratics by Factorising",
  "content": "<p>A <strong>quadratic equation</strong> has the form \\(ax^2 + bx + c = 0\\). To solve by factorising:</p><p>1. Rearrange so one side equals zero.</p><p>2. Factorise.</p><p>3. Set each bracket = 0 and solve.</p><p>This works because if \\(A \\times B = 0\\), then \\(A = 0\\) or \\(B = 0\\).</p>",
  "example": "<p><strong>Solve</strong> \\(x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0\\)</p><p>\\((x-2)(x-3) = 0\\)</p><p>\\(x = 2\\) or \\(x = 3\\)</p>"
 },
